# FENCE.I with a non-coherent I-cache and write-back D-cache: a committed store that
# patches an instruction becomes visible to fetch only through the FENCE.I sequence
# (StoreBuffer drain, D-cache clean, I-cache invalidate, refetch). The patched word is
# addi x5, x0, 7 (0x00700293) over addi x5, x0, 1.
@name ooo-fence-i-self-modifying-code
@verifies funcSystemOpSequencing funcICacheInvalidate funcDCacheCleanAll funcDrainFence funcDCacheWriteback
@verifies funcICacheMissFill funcInstBusGet
@maxcycles 8000
li x6, 0x00700293
jal x28, patch
target: addi x5, x0, 1
jal x0, after
patch: sw x6, 0(x28)
fence.i
jalr x0, x28, 0
after: check x5 == 7
